WEBVTT

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.647
Incredible.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.312
Absolutely thrilling.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.844
All I can say is... wow!

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:25.756
What about you, Mr. Vulcan?

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.487
Isn't that just?

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:28.926
Wow!

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:31.294
Your inarticulate
expression of awe

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:33.196
notwithstanding, Mr. Neelix,

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:35.292
it was a fascinating spectacle.

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.997
That's the edge
of the shock wave.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.902
The pressure's
over 90 kilopascals...

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.497
30 percent more
than we predicted.

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:42.667
Tom, back us off
at full impulse.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:45.177
I want to stay
ahead of the brunt of that wave.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.178
Yes, ma'am.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:47.907
Congratulations, everyone.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:51.007
Only two other crews
in the history of Starfleet

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:53.484
have witnessed
a supernova explosion.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.112
But neither one was this close...

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:56.816
less than ten billion
kilometers...

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.016
definitely a record.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.785
Who brought the champagne?

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.555
Champagne?! Captain, if I
thought you wanted champagne...

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:02.561
Relax, Neelix.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:03.721
It's a figure of speech.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:06.163
Thanks for inviting us
to watch with you, Captain.

00:01:06.199 --> 00:01:07.325
It's really gotten me interested

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.460
in learning more
about stellar phenomena.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:12.528
Just remember, Kes, anyone
can stargaze on the Bridge...

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.665
even a hologram
with a mobile emitter...

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.504
but the real action will
always be in Sick Bay.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.076
How'd those shield modifications
hold up, B'Elanna?

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:22.707
Less than
a seven percent power drain.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:23.716
Good job.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.240
Chakotay, what do you say
we get started

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:26.946
analyzing those carbon
conversion readings?

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.214
Captain, you've been
on the Bridge

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:29.221
for 14 straight hours.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.882
Don't you think you
deserve a little rest?

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.449
Harry and I will get to work
on the astrometric analysis

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.688
and we'll give you a full
report in the morning.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:38.526
You win.
I'll see you at 0700.

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:53.772
Janeway to Security.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.007
Intruder alert.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:57.640
There's no need to call
room service, Kathy.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:58.912
I've already ordered.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.579
Oh, Q.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.713
You did say
you wanted champagne.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:05.952
Janeway to Security.
Intruder alert.

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:07.254
Oh, it's no use.

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.557
I've taken the proverbial phone
off the hook.

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:12.429
After all, we don't want
any interruptions.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:13.864
What are you doing here?

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.731
To us.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.736
There is no us, Q.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:22.400
The night is young,
and the sheets... are satin.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.307
I want you out, but first,
get rid of this bed.

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:26.539
I have no intention
of getting between

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:28.308
those Starfleet-issue sheets.

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:29.975
They give me a terrible rash.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.983
Since you won't
be getting in the bed,

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.417
I wouldn't worry about it.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:36.786
Oh, Kathy...
don't be such a prude.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.916
Admit it.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.983
It has been a while.

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:42.994
And it's going to be
a while longer.

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:43.994
Now get out.

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.086
So tense.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:49.363
Why don't you slip
into something more comfortable?

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:54.340
If you think this puerile
attempt at seduction

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:56.239
is going to work, you're

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:58.267
even more self-deluded
than I thought.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:00.811
Oh, I see.

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:04.749
You think I'm interested
in some tawdry one-night stand.

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:07.810
That's because I haven't
told you why I'm here yet.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:10.618
Out of all the females,
of all the species

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:14.787
in all the galaxies,
I have chosen you

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:18.524
to be the mother of my child.

00:05:07.005 --> 00:05:09.838
I know that you're
probably asking yourself:

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:11.809
"Why would
a brilliant, handsome,

00:05:11.843 --> 00:05:15.210
"dashingly omnipotent being
like Q want to mate

00:05:15.247 --> 00:05:18.341
with a scrawny, little
bipedal specimen like me?"

00:05:18.383 --> 00:05:19.509
Let me guess.

00:05:19.551 --> 00:05:21.644
No one else in the universe
will have you.

00:05:21.686 --> 00:05:23.244
Nonsense!

00:05:23.288 --> 00:05:25.756
I could have chosen
a Klingon targ,

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:28.850
the Romulan empress,
a Cyrillian microbe.

00:05:28.894 --> 00:05:32.159
Really? I beat out
a single-celled organism?

00:05:32.197 --> 00:05:33.494
How flattering.

00:05:33.531 --> 00:05:35.829
It's an overwhelming honor,
isn't it?

00:05:35.867 --> 00:05:37.732
I can't get you out of my mind.

00:05:37.769 --> 00:05:39.896
You're confident,
passionate, beautiful.

00:05:39.938 --> 00:05:41.599
And totally uninterested.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.972
Kathy, you can't leave.

00:05:44.042 --> 00:05:48.206
My cosmic clock is ticking.

00:05:48.246 --> 00:05:51.773
Besides, you have no idea
what you're missing.

00:05:51.816 --> 00:05:55.718
Foreplay with a Q
can last for decades.

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:59.986
Sorry, but I'm busy
for the next 60 or 70 years.

00:06:00.091 --> 00:06:03.788
Oh, I see. This is one
of those silly human rituals.

00:06:03.828 --> 00:06:05.659
You're playing hard to get.

00:06:05.697 --> 00:06:08.666
As far as you're concerned, Q,
I'm impossible to get.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:11.328
Goody. A challenge.

00:06:11.369 --> 00:06:13.360
This is going to be fun.

00:06:21.446 --> 00:06:23.380
Janeway to Bridge.

00:06:23.415 --> 00:06:24.848
Chakotay here, Captain.

00:06:24.883 --> 00:06:26.714
I thought you were going
to get some sleep.

00:06:26.751 --> 00:06:28.912
I've just had a visit from Q.

00:06:28.954 --> 00:06:32.287
He's gone now, but I want
to be notified immediately

00:06:32.324 --> 00:06:34.155
if he reappears
anywhere on the ship,

00:06:34.192 --> 00:06:35.955
or if anything odd
starts to happen.

00:06:36.061 --> 00:06:37.187
Acknowledged.

00:06:37.228 --> 00:06:39.025
What did he want?

00:06:40.665 --> 00:06:43.429
Let's just say he had
a personal request.

00:06:43.468 --> 00:06:44.560
Captain?

00:06:44.602 --> 00:06:47.093
I'm not sure
what he's really up to,

00:06:47.138 --> 00:06:48.799
but I have a feeling
he'll be back.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.171
Janeway out.

00:07:03.822 --> 00:07:05.221
Come in.

00:07:05.256 --> 00:07:08.692
I've got those carbon conversion
readings from the supernova.

00:07:08.727 --> 00:07:10.160
Thank you.

00:07:12.030 --> 00:07:13.520
Is there something else?

00:07:13.565 --> 00:07:16.398
Have you heard
anything more from Q?

00:07:16.434 --> 00:07:17.594
No.

00:07:17.635 --> 00:07:21.036
I wish I could believe
he's gone for good.

00:07:21.072 --> 00:07:23.540
I was wondering
just what you meant

00:07:23.575 --> 00:07:26.237
when you said he made
a personal request.

00:07:29.681 --> 00:07:31.808
He wants to mate with me.

00:07:34.152 --> 00:07:36.916
I see.

00:07:36.955 --> 00:07:38.786
Obviously, it's
out of the question...

00:07:38.823 --> 00:07:41.155
and I suspect
it's a smoke screen, knowing Q.

00:07:41.192 --> 00:07:43.160
He's probably got
some hidden agenda.

00:07:43.194 --> 00:07:44.957
Maybe.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:46.429
Chakotay...

00:07:46.464 --> 00:07:49.092
I know I don't have
any right to feel this way,

00:07:49.134 --> 00:07:51.364
but this bothers
the hell out of me.

00:07:51.403 --> 00:07:53.234
I do believe you're jealous.

00:07:53.271 --> 00:07:55.296
Why didn't you tell me
there was another man?

00:07:56.341 --> 00:07:57.365
Because there isn't.

00:07:57.409 --> 00:07:59.707
I'm just not interested in you.

00:07:59.744 --> 00:08:01.507
Any more questions?

00:08:01.546 --> 00:08:05.038
I was wondering, Kathy,
what could anyone possibly see

00:08:05.083 --> 00:08:06.607
in this big oaf anyway?

00:08:06.651 --> 00:08:07.913
Is it the tattoo?

00:08:08.019 --> 00:08:11.079
Because mine's bigger.

00:08:11.122 --> 00:08:13.750
Not big enough.

00:08:25.236 --> 00:08:28.535
Captain's Log, Stardate 50384.2.

00:08:28.573 --> 00:08:30.564
Q's unannounced visits continue.

00:08:30.608 --> 00:08:32.098
Since I suspect
he's up to something more

00:08:32.143 --> 00:08:33.440
than pursuing me,

00:08:33.478 --> 00:08:35.605
I've instructed the crew
to take every opportunity

00:08:35.647 --> 00:08:36.978
to uncover his true motives.

00:08:38.516 --> 00:08:41.508
Who says crew performance
reports have to be a chore?

00:08:42.921 --> 00:08:45.048
Oh... Sure beats
working on the Bridge.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:46.557
Now, if we could just convince

00:08:46.591 --> 00:08:49.492
the Captain to start holding
morning briefings in here...

00:08:49.527 --> 00:08:50.721
Now, that'll be the day.

00:08:52.797 --> 00:08:54.924
Nice program, Tommy,
but it's all

00:08:54.966 --> 00:08:57.491
just so much hollow
pleasure, isn't it?

00:08:57.535 --> 00:08:59.867
All right, Q, we'll bite.
What do you want?

00:09:02.574 --> 00:09:04.565
Guys...

00:09:04.609 --> 00:09:07.134
I just don't understand
your Captain.

00:09:07.178 --> 00:09:10.670
I've tried everything...
filling the Bridge with roses,

00:09:10.715 --> 00:09:13.650
writing Drabian love sonnets,
serenading her in her bath...

00:09:13.685 --> 00:09:15.846
Oh, I'll bet she loved that one.

00:09:15.887 --> 00:09:18.321
But no matter what lengths I go
to win her heart,

00:09:18.356 --> 00:09:20.347
she rejects me... me!

00:09:20.391 --> 00:09:22.325
How, I ask you,
is that possible?

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:24.590
Did it ever occur to you
that she just doesn't like you?

00:09:25.663 --> 00:09:27.187
No.

00:09:27.232 --> 00:09:29.632
Look, Q, we've been told

00:09:29.667 --> 00:09:32.101
about your appearances
on the Enterprise.

00:09:32.137 --> 00:09:34.731
We know your little visits
usually turn out

00:09:34.772 --> 00:09:36.296
to be more than meet the eye,

00:09:36.341 --> 00:09:38.036
so save
your broken-heart routine

00:09:38.076 --> 00:09:40.067
and tell us
what you're really after.

00:09:44.749 --> 00:09:47.183
I just thought
that the two of you

00:09:47.218 --> 00:09:48.549
might be able to give me
some advice

00:09:48.586 --> 00:09:51.714
on how to break through
Kathy's icy exterior.

00:09:51.756 --> 00:09:54.589
You know, man-to-man.

00:09:57.695 --> 00:10:00.323
My advice would be to give up

00:10:00.365 --> 00:10:03.391
before you embarrass yourself
any more than you already have.

00:10:04.903 --> 00:10:05.961
Come on, Harry.

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:08.265
We're not going to get a
straight answer out of this guy.

00:10:17.815 --> 00:10:24.152
You... bar rodent... another one
of these... fruity concoctions.

00:10:24.189 --> 00:10:26.487
Not unless you tell me

00:10:26.524 --> 00:10:29.118
why you're bothering
Captain Janeway.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:30.286
Captain Janeway?!

00:10:30.328 --> 00:10:32.296
Now, that's a subject
I want to discuss.

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:35.458
Tell me, what are some
of her favorite things?

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.331
Chocolate truffles,
stuffed animals?

00:10:37.368 --> 00:10:39.233
Erotic art?

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:42.330
You can't bribe Captain Janeway.

00:10:42.373 --> 00:10:44.000
Oh, no?
Isn't that what you do?

00:10:44.108 --> 00:10:46.133
What are you talking about?

00:10:46.177 --> 00:10:49.010
I understand that you
acquire things for her...

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.571
create little
interesting diversions,

00:10:51.616 --> 00:10:53.948
prepare little tasty treats.

00:10:53.985 --> 00:10:58.285
After all, why else
would she be so fond of your...

00:10:58.323 --> 00:11:00.655
fur-lined face?

00:11:00.692 --> 00:11:04.423
Do you want to know what Captain
Janeway likes about me?

00:11:04.462 --> 00:11:05.690
I'll tell you.

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:10.326
I am respectful, loyal,
and most of all, sincere,

00:11:10.368 --> 00:11:12.165
and those are qualities
which someone like you

00:11:12.203 --> 00:11:13.898
could never hope to possess.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:54.904
This isn't going to work, Q.

00:11:54.946 --> 00:11:57.847
How can you ignore that face?

00:11:57.882 --> 00:12:00.715
He's adorable,
but this has to stop.

00:12:00.752 --> 00:12:01.810
Please.

00:12:01.853 --> 00:12:03.684
Accept him...

00:12:03.721 --> 00:12:05.848
as a small token
of my affection.

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:07.255
No.

00:12:07.292 --> 00:12:08.520
Suit yourself.

00:12:08.559 --> 00:12:09.753
May we talk?

00:12:09.794 --> 00:12:11.625
Just talk?

00:12:42.427 --> 00:12:47.228
I'm... afraid that I
haven't been sincere.

00:12:47.265 --> 00:12:49.096
When you first asked

00:12:49.133 --> 00:12:51.397
why I wanted to have
a child with you,

00:12:51.436 --> 00:12:54.963
I made jokes,
bragged about my prowess,

00:12:55.006 --> 00:12:56.837
engaged in sexual innuendo.

00:12:56.874 --> 00:12:59.843
I was using all that
to cover up my true feelings.

00:12:59.976 --> 00:13:03.639
And I suppose you want to share
your true feelings with me now.

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:06.911
I'm lonely.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:08.417
Lonely?

00:13:08.451 --> 00:13:10.282
Oh, I know it's hard to believe,

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:13.255
but I've been single
for billions of years.

00:13:13.289 --> 00:13:16.918
It was fun at first...
gallivanting around the galaxy,

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:21.021
using my omnipotence to impress
females of every species.

00:13:23.466 --> 00:13:27.425
The fact of the matter is,
it... it left me empty.

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:30.803
I want someone
to love me for myself.

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:37.336
I guess what I'm saying is...
I want a relationship.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:40.975
I just thought
if you and I had a child,

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:44.816
it would give me that kind
of stability and security

00:13:44.854 --> 00:13:46.981
that I've been missing.

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:48.387
Sorry, Q.

00:13:48.424 --> 00:13:51.257
I'm not buying it.

00:13:51.294 --> 00:13:52.283
Oh.

00:13:52.328 --> 00:13:53.295
All right.

00:13:53.329 --> 00:13:56.093
Let's see if you buy this.

00:14:00.136 --> 00:14:03.503
You're stuck out here, thousands
of light-years from home,

00:14:03.539 --> 00:14:07.475
and you aren't getting
any younger, are you?

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:09.740
All your hopes for home,
hearth or family

00:14:09.779 --> 00:14:11.872
grow dimmer every day.

00:14:11.915 --> 00:14:13.610
Admit it, Kathryn.

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:15.811
You're lonely, too.

00:14:15.852 --> 00:14:19.948
And you wonder if you
will ever have a child.

00:14:20.056 --> 00:14:22.388
You're right.

00:14:22.425 --> 00:14:24.893
I would like to have
a child someday.

00:14:24.928 --> 00:14:25.724
Oh...

00:14:25.762 --> 00:14:27.127
But not with you.

00:14:27.163 --> 00:14:28.221
Why not?

00:14:28.264 --> 00:14:29.253
I'm just not

00:14:29.299 --> 00:14:31.130
the right kind of woman
for you, Q.

00:14:31.167 --> 00:14:34.227
Truer words were never spoken.

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:36.670
Q! How did you find me?

00:14:36.706 --> 00:14:38.139
Never mind that.

00:14:38.174 --> 00:14:40.335
What are you doing
with that dog?

00:14:42.078 --> 00:14:44.808
I'm not talking about the puppy.

00:14:49.252 --> 00:14:51.914
Can't you see I'm busy here?

00:14:51.955 --> 00:14:53.252
Stop stalking me!

00:14:53.289 --> 00:14:55.883
You should be back
in the Continuum.

00:14:55.925 --> 00:14:57.256
Excuse me...

00:14:57.293 --> 00:14:59.488
but who are you exactly?

00:14:59.529 --> 00:15:02.930
Kathryn Janeway,
may I present... Q.

00:15:02.999 --> 00:15:06.560
Not just any Q... his Q.

00:15:06.602 --> 00:15:08.797
We were involved for a while.

00:15:08.838 --> 00:15:11.204
About four billion years.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:14.607
And now you desert me
to pollute the Continuum

00:15:14.644 --> 00:15:18.546
with the DNA of this...
narrow little being.

00:15:18.581 --> 00:15:21.175
I never said it was exclusive.

00:15:21.217 --> 00:15:22.514
Stay away from him.

00:15:22.552 --> 00:15:24.520
Look...

00:15:24.554 --> 00:15:27.250
Miss Q, I'll save you
a lot of trouble.

00:15:27.290 --> 00:15:29.258
I have zero interest in him.

00:15:29.292 --> 00:15:31.419
Oh, now you see
what you've done?

00:15:31.461 --> 00:15:34.259
And I was finally
making progress.

00:15:34.297 --> 00:15:35.730
Bridge to Janeway.

00:15:35.765 --> 00:15:37.232
You'd better come in here,
Captain.

00:15:37.266 --> 00:15:38.233
On my way.

00:15:38.267 --> 00:15:39.632
I'd really appreciate it

00:15:39.669 --> 00:15:42.729
if you would take this
domestic squabble off my ship.

00:15:49.312 --> 00:15:50.506
Report.

00:15:50.546 --> 00:15:52.480
You're not going
to believe this, Captain,

00:15:52.515 --> 00:15:54.574
but another star in this cluster
just went supernova.

00:15:54.617 --> 00:15:56.983
It's.02 light-years
from our current position.

00:15:57.053 --> 00:15:59.351
Make that two supernovas,
Commander...

00:15:59.389 --> 00:16:02.256
I just picked up another one
at 217 mark 47.

00:16:02.291 --> 00:16:04.919
Estimated time of implosion:
67 seconds.

00:16:04.961 --> 00:16:06.690
Get us out of here, Tom.

00:16:06.729 --> 00:16:07.923
I can't.
A subspace shock wave

00:16:07.964 --> 00:16:09.795
from the star is
collapsing the warp field.

00:16:09.832 --> 00:16:10.924
Red Alert.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:12.934
Tuvok, increase power
to the shields.

00:16:13.002 --> 00:16:15.562
Tom, lay in a course
away from that shock wave,

00:16:15.605 --> 00:16:16.731
maximum impulse.

00:16:16.773 --> 00:16:19.241
A star going supernova
is an event that occurs

00:16:19.275 --> 00:16:21.140
once every century
in this galaxy.

00:16:21.177 --> 00:16:23.202
Now we're about to witness
our third

00:16:23.246 --> 00:16:25.874
in less than three days...
all in the same sector.

00:16:25.915 --> 00:16:28.884
Why do I suspect you
have something to do with this?

00:16:28.918 --> 00:16:30.044
She may be a member

00:16:30.086 --> 00:16:32.680
of an intellectually
challenged species,

00:16:32.722 --> 00:16:33.746
but she's right.

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:35.655
Your irresponsible behavior

00:16:35.691 --> 00:16:38.455
is continuing
to have cosmic consequences.

00:16:38.494 --> 00:16:40.655
Will you stop overreacting?!

00:16:40.696 --> 00:16:41.856
Always nagging.

00:16:41.898 --> 00:16:44.093
Now you see why I left her.

00:16:44.133 --> 00:16:45.930
Are you causing
these supernovas?

00:16:45.968 --> 00:16:48.300
Well, not exactly.

00:16:48.337 --> 00:16:49.827
What's that supposed to mean?

00:16:49.872 --> 00:16:50.930
It's no use, Captain.

00:16:50.973 --> 00:16:52.463
The shock wave
is too fast for us.

00:16:52.508 --> 00:16:54.100
Try evasive maneuvers.

00:16:54.143 --> 00:16:56.111
I'm afraid a course correction
will be futile, Captain.

00:16:56.145 --> 00:16:57.908
There are now
three distinct shock waves

00:16:57.947 --> 00:17:00.142
heading toward us
on various trajectories.

00:17:00.183 --> 00:17:02.310
It will be impossible
to avoid them all.

00:17:02.351 --> 00:17:04.478
Divert auxiliary power
to the shields.

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:06.579
You have the ability to get
us out of here, so do it.

00:17:06.622 --> 00:17:07.782
16 seconds to impact.

00:17:07.824 --> 00:17:09.917
I'm not sure if the shields
will hold.

00:17:09.992 --> 00:17:11.721
Do something, Q!

00:17:11.761 --> 00:17:14.594
Well...

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:15.824
if you insist.

00:17:17.867 --> 00:17:20.267
That two-timing toad!

00:17:21.804 --> 00:17:23.135
Contact
with the first shock wave

00:17:23.172 --> 00:17:24.503
within three seconds, Commander.

00:17:24.540 --> 00:17:26.303
All hands, brace for impact.

00:17:40.356 --> 00:17:43.120
Q, where have you taken me?

00:17:59.342 --> 00:18:02.903
Well, I must admit
your gown is very becoming.

00:18:03.012 --> 00:18:05.674
I don't have time
for your little fantasies.

00:18:05.715 --> 00:18:07.012
Return me to Voyager.

00:18:07.049 --> 00:18:08.846
This is no fantasy.

00:18:08.885 --> 00:18:11.718
You're in the Q Continuum now.

00:18:11.754 --> 00:18:13.051
The Continuum?

00:18:13.089 --> 00:18:14.920
That's right.

00:18:16.492 --> 00:18:18.824
I'm simply allowing you
to perceive it in the context

00:18:18.861 --> 00:18:20.488
your human mind can comprehend.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:22.828
The last time
you brought me here,

00:18:22.865 --> 00:18:25.493
it looked like
some sort of way station

00:18:25.535 --> 00:18:26.661
on a desert road.

00:18:26.702 --> 00:18:29.330
Ha. It was awfully drab,
wasn't it?

00:18:29.372 --> 00:18:32.933
But this... this is
a much more colorful

00:18:32.975 --> 00:18:34.943
representation for a human

00:18:34.977 --> 00:18:37.138
of American descent,
don't you think?

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:38.579
An elegant manor house,

00:18:38.614 --> 00:18:40.047
a beautiful southern belle,

00:18:40.082 --> 00:18:43.108
a dashing Union officer,
determined to win her affections

00:18:43.152 --> 00:18:45.416
despite her hatred
for Yankee interlopers...

00:18:45.454 --> 00:18:48.651
Enough. The only thing
that interests me right now

00:18:48.691 --> 00:18:50.955
is the welfare
of my ship and crew.

00:18:50.993 --> 00:18:52.961
Well, I'm sure
your First Officer...

00:18:52.995 --> 00:18:54.189
Chuckles, is it?

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:57.722
I'm sure he's got everything
under control for the moment.

00:18:57.767 --> 00:19:01.032
I'd like to make sure of that
myself, if you don't mind.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.868
This has gone
way beyond your ship.

00:19:03.906 --> 00:19:06.704
It's even gone
beyond you and me.

00:19:06.742 --> 00:19:10.906
This is about the future
of the Continuum itself.

00:19:10.947 --> 00:19:14.508
Stop speaking in riddles
and tell me what's going on.

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:16.575
I'll do better than that.

00:19:16.619 --> 00:19:18.280
I'll show you.

00:19:25.461 --> 00:19:27.452
The Continuum is burning.

00:19:27.496 --> 00:19:30.727
The Q are in the middle
of a civil war.

00:19:38.374 --> 00:19:39.841
Start explaining.

00:19:39.875 --> 00:19:42.571
Do you remember our friend
Quinn?

00:19:43.946 --> 00:19:46.847
The Q who committed suicide
aboard Voyager?

00:19:46.882 --> 00:19:49.350
Do you recall
what I said might happen

00:19:49.385 --> 00:19:51.945
if he were allowed
to take his own life?

00:19:51.988 --> 00:19:53.785
You said it would represent

00:19:53.823 --> 00:19:56.121
an interruption
to the Continuum...

00:19:56.158 --> 00:19:58.956
that it could have
dire consequences.

00:19:59.061 --> 00:20:01.757
I'd say a civil war
is pretty dire, wouldn't you?

00:20:01.797 --> 00:20:04.664
His death caused this conflict.

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:08.659
It caused chaos and upheaval...

00:20:08.704 --> 00:20:10.763
because even though he was gone,

00:20:10.806 --> 00:20:13.400
his calls for freedom
and individualism

00:20:13.442 --> 00:20:15.933
continued to echo
in the ears of those

00:20:15.978 --> 00:20:17.878
who believed in his teachings...

00:20:17.913 --> 00:20:19.380
myself among them.

00:20:19.415 --> 00:20:22.646
I sounded the trumpet
and carried the banner.

00:20:22.685 --> 00:20:24.653
Naturally, others followed.

00:20:24.687 --> 00:20:26.518
The forces of the status quo

00:20:26.555 --> 00:20:28.853
tried to crush us
once and for all,

00:20:28.891 --> 00:20:30.188
but we fought back

00:20:30.226 --> 00:20:33.354
and now there's a cosmic
struggle for supremacy

00:20:33.396 --> 00:20:37.355
and the battle is spreading,
causing hazardous repercussions

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:38.890
throughout the galaxy.

00:20:38.934 --> 00:20:40.401
Oh, the supernovas.

00:20:41.437 --> 00:20:44.406
You might call them...

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:46.704
"galactic cross fire."

00:20:48.277 --> 00:20:49.835
It's terrible, isn't it?

00:20:49.879 --> 00:20:52.347
But it's also
a wonderful opportunity.

00:20:52.381 --> 00:20:55.646
I fail to see anything
wonderful about a war.

00:20:55.685 --> 00:20:57.846
War can be an engine of change.

00:20:57.887 --> 00:21:00.321
War can transform
a society for the better.

00:21:00.356 --> 00:21:02.654
Your own civil war
brought about an end

00:21:02.692 --> 00:21:04.192
to slavery and oppression.

00:21:04.325 --> 00:21:07.852
But our civil war came at a time
before mankind had learned

00:21:07.895 --> 00:21:10.125
to resolve disputes
without bloodshed.

00:21:10.164 --> 00:21:12.359
Surely, the Q have evolved
to a point

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:14.595
where you can find
a nonviolent way

00:21:14.635 --> 00:21:15.932
to resolve a conflict.

00:21:15.970 --> 00:21:17.699
That's where you come in.

00:21:17.738 --> 00:21:19.603
What do I have to do
with any of this, Q?

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:21.938
I want you to help me
transform the Continuum

00:21:21.976 --> 00:21:24.706
in the same way your civil war
transformed a nation.

00:21:24.745 --> 00:21:26.110
By mating with you?!

00:21:26.147 --> 00:21:27.205
I know.

00:21:27.248 --> 00:21:28.738
It's brilliant, isn't it?

00:21:28.783 --> 00:21:31.877
I don't see how a baby
is going to end a war

00:21:31.919 --> 00:21:34.945
being fought by a race
of omnipotent beings.

00:21:34.989 --> 00:21:36.286
It's simple.

00:21:36.324 --> 00:21:38.554
Mating will create
a new breed of Q,

00:21:38.593 --> 00:21:39.753
which will combine

00:21:39.794 --> 00:21:42.160
my omnipotence
and infinite intellect

00:21:42.196 --> 00:21:44.756
with the best that humanity
has to offer.

00:21:44.799 --> 00:21:48.963
You believe human DNA
is going to restore peace?

00:21:49.003 --> 00:21:50.300
Precisely.

00:21:50.338 --> 00:21:52.772
What the Continuum needs
right now

00:21:52.807 --> 00:21:54.934
is an infusion of fresh blood,

00:21:54.976 --> 00:21:58.412
a new sensibility,
a new leader, a new messiah.

00:22:01.382 --> 00:22:02.349
Think of it, Kathy...

00:22:02.383 --> 00:22:04.442
our child will be
like a precious stone

00:22:04.485 --> 00:22:06.214
tossed into the cosmic lake,

00:22:06.254 --> 00:22:07.721
sending endless ripples

00:22:07.755 --> 00:22:09.882
of human conscience
and compassion

00:22:09.924 --> 00:22:13.052
to wash up on every distant
shore of the universe.

00:22:13.094 --> 00:22:14.686
What greater contribution

00:22:14.729 --> 00:22:16.924
could a being
of your limited power

00:22:16.964 --> 00:22:18.158
ever hope to make?

00:22:18.199 --> 00:22:21.760
What is more important
to humanity than peace?

00:22:21.802 --> 00:22:27.001
I'm offering you the opportunity
to be the mother of peace.

00:22:31.312 --> 00:22:33.780
Well, what's it going to be?

00:22:36.484 --> 00:22:37.610
Q!

00:22:40.154 --> 00:22:42.145
You're bleeding.

00:22:59.040 --> 00:23:00.439
Report!

00:23:00.474 --> 00:23:02.442
Shield strength
is at 20 percent.

00:23:02.476 --> 00:23:05.172
Hull damage
on Decks 9 through 14.

00:23:05.212 --> 00:23:07.510
Minor injuries reported
on all decks.

00:23:07.548 --> 00:23:09.106
Warp drive is off-line.

00:23:09.150 --> 00:23:10.549
Commander, according
to these readings,

00:23:10.584 --> 00:23:12.882
the shock waves have
knocked us 16 billion

00:23:12.920 --> 00:23:14.854
kilometers
from our previous location.

00:23:18.192 --> 00:23:19.454
I want to know
what's going on here.

00:23:19.493 --> 00:23:20.619
Where's Captain Janeway?

00:23:20.661 --> 00:23:24.097
Let me go before I hurl
this ship and everyone on it

00:23:24.131 --> 00:23:25.826
into the Therinian Ice Age.

00:23:25.866 --> 00:23:27.424
I don't think you can.

00:23:27.468 --> 00:23:29.129
Don't be ridiculous.

00:23:30.171 --> 00:23:31.365
I don't know how or why,

00:23:31.405 --> 00:23:33.270
but something's
affected your powers.

00:23:33.307 --> 00:23:34.604
Otherwise, you wouldn't
still be here

00:23:34.642 --> 00:23:36.337
and you wouldn't have
a bruise on your forehead.

00:23:36.377 --> 00:23:39.744
Now start talking
before I hurl you into the brig.

00:23:45.519 --> 00:23:47.612
And it's the war
in the Continuum

00:23:47.655 --> 00:23:49.418
that's causing the supernovas?

00:23:49.457 --> 00:23:50.685
May we presume

00:23:50.725 --> 00:23:52.454
that this conflict
is also responsible

00:23:52.493 --> 00:23:54.256
for the weakening of your powers

00:23:54.295 --> 00:23:56.729
and your inability
to return to the Continuum?

00:23:56.764 --> 00:23:59.164
The Vulcan talent
for stating the obvious

00:23:59.200 --> 00:24:00.633
never ceases to amaze me.

00:24:00.668 --> 00:24:03.796
How were Q and Captain Janeway
able to reenter the Continuum,

00:24:03.838 --> 00:24:04.862
and you weren't?

00:24:04.905 --> 00:24:07.931
I tried to return, but I was
wounded in the process.

00:24:07.975 --> 00:24:09.636
Oh.
Don't try to understand it.

00:24:09.677 --> 00:24:12.942
It's far beyond your limited
capacity to comprehend.

00:24:12.980 --> 00:24:14.106
What's important is,

00:24:14.148 --> 00:24:15.945
I'm stuck here with you mortals

00:24:16.050 --> 00:24:18.075
while Q is probably
in the process

00:24:18.119 --> 00:24:22.112
of irreparably harming the
Continuum with that woman.

00:24:22.156 --> 00:24:27.287
Hmm! Tossed aside for someone
five billion years younger.

00:24:27.328 --> 00:24:30.126
If it weren't so
laughable, I'd cry.

00:24:30.164 --> 00:24:32.291
Look, we want our Captain back,

00:24:32.333 --> 00:24:34.824
and you obviously
want to get home.

00:24:34.869 --> 00:24:36.962
Why don't we help each other?

00:24:37.004 --> 00:24:39.472
How could you possibly help me?

00:24:39.507 --> 00:24:42.943
There's got to be some way
to get back to the Continuum

00:24:42.977 --> 00:24:44.808
besides snapping your fingers.

00:24:44.845 --> 00:24:48.144
Hmm. Well, there
is one possibility,

00:24:48.182 --> 00:24:50.912
but, somehow, I don't think
this rickety barge

00:24:50.951 --> 00:24:53.078
or your half-witted
crew members

00:24:53.120 --> 00:24:54.644
are up to the challenge.

00:24:54.688 --> 00:24:56.485
May I remind you, madam,

00:24:56.524 --> 00:24:58.389
that this "rickety barge"

00:24:58.426 --> 00:25:00.257
and its "half-witted crew"

00:25:00.294 --> 00:25:02.125
are your only hope
at the moment.

00:25:14.742 --> 00:25:16.039
Ow!

00:25:16.076 --> 00:25:17.373
That hurts.

00:25:17.411 --> 00:25:18.708
Be still.

00:25:18.746 --> 00:25:21.112
I never thought
a Q could be injured.

00:25:21.148 --> 00:25:23.582
As I said, this is
only your perception

00:25:23.617 --> 00:25:24.948
of what is happening.

00:25:27.955 --> 00:25:31.254
I can assure you
those are not mere cannon balls

00:25:31.292 --> 00:25:33.453
and lead charges
being fired at us.

00:25:33.494 --> 00:25:35.860
So they're some sort of...

00:25:35.896 --> 00:25:37.193
Q weapons?

00:25:37.231 --> 00:25:40.223
You'd be surprised
what innovative munitions

00:25:40.267 --> 00:25:42.735
can be created
by one immortal being

00:25:42.770 --> 00:25:45.170
who set his mind
on killing another.

00:25:45.206 --> 00:25:47.333
Hold your fire!
Hold your fire!

00:25:47.374 --> 00:25:48.602
You're surrounded, Q.

00:25:48.642 --> 00:25:51.543
Surrender now,
and we'll be merciful.

00:25:51.579 --> 00:25:53.206
Call a truce. Talk to them.

00:25:53.247 --> 00:25:55.613
Maybe you can
resolve this peacefully.

00:25:55.649 --> 00:25:57.776
What's your answer, Q?

00:26:13.934 --> 00:26:15.925
I'll never surrender,
you know that!

00:26:15.970 --> 00:26:18.063
Resume fire!
Resume fire!

00:26:20.274 --> 00:26:21.935
Get the rifle in the corner.

00:26:22.009 --> 00:26:23.237
And take the other window.

00:26:23.277 --> 00:26:25.472
This is your fight, Q, not mine.

00:26:25.513 --> 00:26:26.605
That's how you feel about it.

00:26:26.647 --> 00:26:28.547
But if their weapons
can make me bleed,

00:26:28.582 --> 00:26:30.743
what do you think
they'll do to you?

00:26:42.663 --> 00:26:44.460
Oh!

00:26:44.498 --> 00:26:47.023
Q... come on.

00:26:49.069 --> 00:26:50.366
Come on!

00:26:59.113 --> 00:27:02.810
First Officer's Log,
Stardate 50392.7.

00:27:02.850 --> 00:27:04.112
While we don't fully understand

00:27:04.151 --> 00:27:05.709
the astrophysics
underlying her plan,

00:27:05.753 --> 00:27:08.916
the female Q has suggested
several modifications

00:27:09.023 --> 00:27:11.821
which may allow Voyager
to enter the Continuum.

00:27:12.960 --> 00:27:14.587
Well?

00:27:14.628 --> 00:27:15.595
Well, what?

00:27:15.629 --> 00:27:16.926
Are you finished yet?

00:27:16.964 --> 00:27:18.397
What you've asked us to do

00:27:18.432 --> 00:27:20.332
requires a complete
reconfiguration

00:27:20.367 --> 00:27:21.425
of the shield array.

00:27:21.468 --> 00:27:22.435
It takes a while...

00:27:22.469 --> 00:27:24.096
for us mere mortals, that is.

00:27:24.138 --> 00:27:26.936
Surely there's some way
you can speed up the process?

00:27:27.041 --> 00:27:28.406
If you're in such a hurry,

00:27:28.442 --> 00:27:30.410
why don't you
just snap your fingers

00:27:30.444 --> 00:27:31.502
and do it yourself?

00:27:31.545 --> 00:27:32.512
Oh, that's right.

00:27:32.546 --> 00:27:35.037
You've lost your powers
and you need our help.

00:27:35.082 --> 00:27:36.640
I don't think you understand.

00:27:36.684 --> 00:27:39.278
It's imperative that I get back
to the Continuum

00:27:39.320 --> 00:27:41.083
before Q mates
with your Captain.

00:27:41.121 --> 00:27:42.349
I understand perfectly.

00:27:42.389 --> 00:27:43.856
You aren't the first female

00:27:43.891 --> 00:27:45.791
who's ever had a man
run out on her.

00:27:45.826 --> 00:27:49.387
I hope you're not comparing
some failed romance

00:27:49.430 --> 00:27:53.958
in your pitiful existence to
my eternal association with Q?

00:27:54.034 --> 00:27:55.899
You know, I have really had it

00:27:55.936 --> 00:27:58.268
with this superiority complex
of yours.

00:27:58.305 --> 00:27:59.932
It's not a complex, dear.

00:27:59.974 --> 00:28:00.941
It's a fact.

00:28:00.975 --> 00:28:02.408
Well, here's another fact:

00:28:02.443 --> 00:28:05.571
If you don't stop pestering me,
I'm never going to finish,

00:28:05.613 --> 00:28:07.843
in which case,
your association with Q

00:28:07.881 --> 00:28:11.942
might not be quite
as eternal as you think.

00:28:13.854 --> 00:28:17.688
You know, I've always liked
Klingon females.

00:28:17.725 --> 00:28:20.023
You've got such... spunk.

00:28:26.467 --> 00:28:28.367
Oh, thank you.

00:28:28.402 --> 00:28:30.393
Yup. Here you go.

00:28:33.507 --> 00:28:35.532
Easy now.
Keep drinking.

00:28:35.576 --> 00:28:37.669
Oh, thank you, thank you.

00:28:37.711 --> 00:28:39.941
Sure thing.
You take as much as you want.

00:28:39.980 --> 00:28:41.208
Ah, yes.

00:28:41.248 --> 00:28:42.215
Take your time.

00:29:01.435 --> 00:29:02.667
Where are we?

00:29:02.800 --> 00:29:05.291
One of your faction's
encampments.

00:29:05.336 --> 00:29:07.361
How?

00:29:07.405 --> 00:29:09.373
I pulled you out of the mansion

00:29:09.407 --> 00:29:12.342
and managed to hide you
from the enemy patrols.

00:29:12.376 --> 00:29:14.469
Then I spotted
some of your people

00:29:14.512 --> 00:29:16.241
retreating from the battle.

00:29:16.280 --> 00:29:21.479
From the look of them, I'd say
you're not on the winning side.

00:29:21.519 --> 00:29:23.851
You saved my life.

00:29:23.888 --> 00:29:26.880
And now, it's time
to end all this.

00:29:26.924 --> 00:29:29.017
I knew you'd come around.

00:29:31.962 --> 00:29:35.125
I've been thinking
about what you said...

00:29:35.166 --> 00:29:39.330
that creating a new Q
could bring an era of peace.

00:29:39.370 --> 00:29:42.168
Oh, my wild, sweet Kathy.

00:29:42.206 --> 00:29:45.573
I promise you won't regret it.

00:29:45.609 --> 00:29:49.101
Oh, you're not going to have
a child with me.

00:29:50.147 --> 00:29:51.239
You're going to mate

00:29:51.282 --> 00:29:53.443
with that charming lady friend
of yours

00:29:53.484 --> 00:29:55.475
that appeared on my ship.

00:29:59.490 --> 00:30:01.958
Mate with another Q?

00:30:01.992 --> 00:30:03.289
Ridiculous.

00:30:03.327 --> 00:30:04.954
Sounded to me

00:30:05.062 --> 00:30:07.257
like you and she had
a very long-term relationship.

00:30:07.298 --> 00:30:09.528
Yes, but it was never physical.

00:30:09.567 --> 00:30:11.899
I mean, the Q
are way beyond sex.

00:30:11.936 --> 00:30:13.460
It's never been done.

00:30:13.504 --> 00:30:14.698
Really?

00:30:14.739 --> 00:30:17.435
Then how exactly did
the Q come into existence

00:30:17.475 --> 00:30:18.635
in the first place?

00:30:18.676 --> 00:30:21.076
The Q didn't come
into existence.

00:30:21.112 --> 00:30:22.977
The Q have always existed.

00:30:23.080 --> 00:30:25.947
Besides, I can only
mate with a species

00:30:25.983 --> 00:30:27.416
capable of copulation...

00:30:27.451 --> 00:30:28.418
like you.

00:30:28.452 --> 00:30:31.421
But I don't love you, Q.

00:30:31.455 --> 00:30:33.821
Yes, but what does that
have to do with it?

00:30:33.858 --> 00:30:35.985
Everything.
It's the foundation of a family.

00:30:36.026 --> 00:30:38.358
I could never have a child
with someone I didn't love,

00:30:38.395 --> 00:30:40.260
much less give it up
to the Continuum.

00:30:40.297 --> 00:30:42.629
Dearest Kathy, I would never
dream of having you give it up.

00:30:42.666 --> 00:30:44.099
I mean, who would raise it?

00:30:44.135 --> 00:30:45.329
Who would look after it?

00:30:45.369 --> 00:30:47.929
I'm really not cut out
to be a wet nurse.

00:30:49.306 --> 00:30:52.469
Oh... so you're not willing
to do the hard work?

00:30:52.510 --> 00:30:54.603
I'm an idea man.

00:30:54.645 --> 00:30:57.239
Hard work isn't my forte.

00:30:57.281 --> 00:30:59.181
I'd change specialties
if I were you,

00:30:59.216 --> 00:31:01.150
'cause the kind of trouble
you're in

00:31:01.185 --> 00:31:02.709
needs more than a quick fix.

00:31:02.753 --> 00:31:04.778
You can't just sprinkle
a little human DNA

00:31:04.822 --> 00:31:07.222
into the Continuum
and make everything all right.

00:31:07.258 --> 00:31:09.726
Why not?

00:31:12.329 --> 00:31:16.265
Those "best qualities
of humanity" you talked about

00:31:16.300 --> 00:31:18.962
aren't a simple matter
of genetics.

00:31:19.036 --> 00:31:22.699
Love, conscience, compassion...

00:31:23.741 --> 00:31:24.708
...they're attributes

00:31:24.742 --> 00:31:27.836
that mankind has developed
over centuries;

00:31:27.878 --> 00:31:30.972
values that have passed
from one generation to the next,

00:31:31.081 --> 00:31:35.643
taught by parents
to their children.

00:31:35.686 --> 00:31:39.918
Creating a new kind of Q
is a noble idea,

00:31:39.957 --> 00:31:41.822
but it will take more
than impregnating someone

00:31:41.859 --> 00:31:43.952
and walking away.

00:31:43.994 --> 00:31:48.260
If you want your offspring
to embrace your ideals,

00:31:48.299 --> 00:31:50.995
you're going to have
to teach them yourself.

00:31:51.101 --> 00:31:53.865
Yes, but that's exactly why
I want you here...

00:31:53.904 --> 00:31:56.168
to nourish and guide
the little tyke.

00:31:56.207 --> 00:31:58.675
Think of the opportunities
here in the Continuum.

00:31:58.709 --> 00:32:02.645
The entire universe would be
our child's playground.

00:32:02.680 --> 00:32:06.377
Together, the two of you
could explore dimensions

00:32:06.417 --> 00:32:08.578
you've never even imagined.

00:32:08.619 --> 00:32:10.052
'Fess up...

00:32:10.087 --> 00:32:13.454
isn't it even slightly tempting?

00:32:14.758 --> 00:32:17.090
I'd be lying if I said no.

00:32:17.127 --> 00:32:19.960
What explorer
wouldn't be intrigued

00:32:19.997 --> 00:32:23.956
by the idea of seeking out
whole new dimensions?

00:32:24.001 --> 00:32:26.799
But I have other
responsibilities

00:32:26.837 --> 00:32:29.397
and I won't just abandon them.

00:32:29.440 --> 00:32:30.600
Ah, yes.

00:32:30.641 --> 00:32:33.906
The crew of the intrepid
Starship Voyager.

00:32:33.944 --> 00:32:38.074
Perhaps you'd be interested
in sending them home.

00:32:38.115 --> 00:32:41.676
You've tempted me
with that prospect before,

00:32:41.719 --> 00:32:46.281
but, frankly, your credibility
is more than a little suspect.

00:32:49.126 --> 00:32:50.787
My crew and I will get home.

00:32:50.828 --> 00:32:52.295
We're committed to that.

00:32:52.329 --> 00:32:53.762
But we're going to do it

00:32:53.797 --> 00:32:55.924
through hard work
and determination.

00:32:55.966 --> 00:32:59.424
We are not looking
for a quick fix.

00:33:02.473 --> 00:33:04.941
Even if I wanted to mate,
I wouldn't know how.

00:33:04.975 --> 00:33:06.465
It's totally unprecedented.

00:33:06.510 --> 00:33:08.102
You'll figure something out.

00:33:08.145 --> 00:33:11.581
You are omnipotent, after all.

00:33:11.615 --> 00:33:13.549
I need time to think about it.

00:33:13.584 --> 00:33:14.551
Time's up, Q.

00:33:14.585 --> 00:33:15.950
You've got to stop this war

00:33:15.986 --> 00:33:17.886
before it destroys
the Continuum.

00:33:17.922 --> 00:33:19.719
Now, I'm taking this white flag

00:33:19.757 --> 00:33:21.850
and I'm going over
to the enemy camp

00:33:21.892 --> 00:33:24.656
and I'm going to tell them
you're ready to talk

00:33:24.695 --> 00:33:26.458
about terms for a cease-fire.

00:33:26.497 --> 00:33:28.965
Kathy, don't be a hero.

00:33:28.999 --> 00:33:31.968
I'm going, Q,

00:33:32.002 --> 00:33:34.971
so if I were you,
I'd start working on a way

00:33:35.005 --> 00:33:36.996
to set that precedent.

00:33:44.315 --> 00:33:46.875
First Officer's Log,
supplemental.

00:33:46.917 --> 00:33:48.782
We've laid in a course
for the point in space

00:33:48.819 --> 00:33:51.083
where the female Q says
we can enter the Continuum

00:33:51.121 --> 00:33:52.520
and find the Captain.

00:33:54.358 --> 00:33:56.258
You... helm boy.

00:33:56.293 --> 00:33:59.387
Adjust course
to heading 235 mark 08.

00:33:59.430 --> 00:34:02.763
Increase speed
to maximum impulse.

00:34:02.800 --> 00:34:03.926
Sir?

00:34:03.968 --> 00:34:05.833
Uh, Commander?

00:34:05.869 --> 00:34:07.769
What is it, Harry?

00:34:07.805 --> 00:34:09.466
She's put us on a direct course

00:34:09.506 --> 00:34:11.440
for another star
about to go supernova.

00:34:11.475 --> 00:34:14.171
You did say you wanted
to get into the Continuum.

00:34:14.211 --> 00:34:15.508
Yes, but in one piece.

00:34:15.546 --> 00:34:17.946
Try to wrap your minuscule mind
around this.

00:34:18.015 --> 00:34:21.314
These supernovas are actually
caused by spatial disruptions

00:34:21.352 --> 00:34:23.843
within the Continuum...
the result of the war.

00:34:23.887 --> 00:34:25.548
Now, each time a star implodes,

00:34:25.589 --> 00:34:27.921
a negative density
false vacuum is created,

00:34:27.958 --> 00:34:30.324
which actually sucks
the surrounding matter

00:34:30.361 --> 00:34:31.453
into the Continuum.

00:34:31.495 --> 00:34:33.258
So Voyager will be pulled in,
too.

00:34:33.297 --> 00:34:34.628
If we time it perfectly.

00:34:34.665 --> 00:34:36.599
Otherwise,
the subsequent explosion

00:34:36.633 --> 00:34:38.624
will blow you all
into micro-fragments.

00:34:38.669 --> 00:34:41.229
Commander, I needn't remind you

00:34:41.271 --> 00:34:43.899
that close proximity
to a supernova will crush us

00:34:43.941 --> 00:34:45.806
whether or not
we time it perfectly.

00:34:46.944 --> 00:34:48.639
You're so negative.

00:34:48.679 --> 00:34:50.203
He does have a point.

00:34:50.247 --> 00:34:51.305
Humanoids.

00:34:51.348 --> 00:34:52.713
Q to Engineering.

00:34:52.750 --> 00:34:54.411
Go ahead, Q.

00:34:54.451 --> 00:34:56.078
Take warp drive off-line,

00:34:56.120 --> 00:34:59.089
then remodulate the shields
to emit a beta-tachyon pulse

00:34:59.123 --> 00:35:01.853
and prepare to emit a series
of focused antiproton beams

00:35:01.892 --> 00:35:02.916
to the shield bubble.

00:35:03.027 --> 00:35:05.188
Does this make any sense
to you at all, B'Elanna?

00:35:05.229 --> 00:35:07.720
I'd be lying if I said
I understood it completely,

00:35:07.765 --> 00:35:10.598
but if she's thinking
what I think she's thinking,

00:35:10.634 --> 00:35:13.467
we should increase power
to the shields by...

00:35:13.504 --> 00:35:15.267
a factor of ten.

00:35:15.305 --> 00:35:17.034
That's assuming, of course,
that the shield bubble

00:35:17.074 --> 00:35:19.099
doesn't ignite
and burn us all to a crisp.

00:35:19.143 --> 00:35:22.271
We'll be reaching the
imploding star in 13 seconds.

00:35:22.312 --> 00:35:24.246
I still have time
to change course.

00:35:25.249 --> 00:35:26.273
Maintain your course.

00:35:26.316 --> 00:35:27.806
B'Elanna,
take warp drive off-line,

00:35:27.851 --> 00:35:29.478
remodulate the shields

00:35:29.520 --> 00:35:30.953
and get ready to emit
the antiprotons.

00:35:31.055 --> 00:35:33.080
Acknowledged.

00:35:37.127 --> 00:35:40.119
Entering the star's corona
in three seconds.

00:35:41.665 --> 00:35:43.496
Antiprotons now, B'Elanna.

00:35:59.183 --> 00:36:02.380
Ah, Captain Janeway, I presume.

00:36:02.419 --> 00:36:03.784
You're dismissed.

00:36:03.821 --> 00:36:06.085
I'm sorry to have kept
you waiting, madam.

00:36:06.123 --> 00:36:08.182
Please, sit down.

00:36:09.693 --> 00:36:13.629
I understand you walked into
our camp alone and unarmed?

00:36:13.664 --> 00:36:15.131
That's right.

00:36:15.165 --> 00:36:17.429
The Continuum is a dangerous
place for all of us right now,

00:36:17.468 --> 00:36:19.663
not to mention
a solitary human female.

00:36:19.703 --> 00:36:21.796
I admire your bravery.

00:36:21.839 --> 00:36:24.501
I've come with an offer
of truce from Q.

00:36:24.541 --> 00:36:28.170
I'm afraid the time
for diplomacy is past, madam.

00:36:28.212 --> 00:36:29.702
If we don't end this war
quickly,

00:36:29.746 --> 00:36:32.943
the damage to subspace
will be... irreversible.

00:36:32.983 --> 00:36:35.315
Then you agree
the fighting has to stop.

00:36:35.352 --> 00:36:36.410
Most certainly.

00:36:36.453 --> 00:36:39.217
That's why we intend to bring
this war to a conclusion

00:36:39.256 --> 00:36:42.089
by the most expedient
means possible.

00:36:42.126 --> 00:36:44.788
I'm relieved
to hear you say that.

00:36:44.828 --> 00:36:47.228
May I ask how?

00:36:47.264 --> 00:36:49.255
Quite simple, really.

00:36:49.299 --> 00:36:50.596
Since Q is the ringleader

00:36:50.634 --> 00:36:52.465
of the so-called
"freedom faction,"

00:36:52.503 --> 00:36:54.664
we shall have to execute him.

00:36:56.106 --> 00:36:58.336
With all due respect, sir,

00:36:58.375 --> 00:37:02.243
there are no chapters
in the history of my own people

00:37:02.279 --> 00:37:05.578
more tragic than wars which set
neighbor against neighbor.

00:37:05.616 --> 00:37:08.517
Q has an idea
for a nonviolent way

00:37:08.552 --> 00:37:10.577
to bring this conflict
to an end.

00:37:10.621 --> 00:37:14.490
I urge you to listen
to what he has to say.

00:37:14.623 --> 00:37:16.614
We're already resolved, madam.

00:37:16.658 --> 00:37:17.920
I'd be greatly in your debt

00:37:18.026 --> 00:37:20.221
if you'd tell me
where we could find him.

00:37:20.262 --> 00:37:22.196
I won't do that.

00:37:22.231 --> 00:37:24.426
No, I didn't think you would.

00:37:24.466 --> 00:37:25.626
Excuse me, sir.

00:37:26.835 --> 00:37:30.532
Fortunately, we won't
be needing your assistance.

00:37:30.572 --> 00:37:31.732
I told you,
he's willing to negotiate.

00:37:31.773 --> 00:37:32.740
Let him go.

00:37:32.774 --> 00:37:33.741
She's right.

00:37:33.775 --> 00:37:34.867
I've had a change of heart.

00:37:34.910 --> 00:37:36.502
Grovel all you want, Q.

00:37:36.545 --> 00:37:39.446
I've been waiting for this
moment for an eternity.

00:37:39.481 --> 00:37:40.846
Put them both in chains.

00:37:40.883 --> 00:37:41.747
Wait.

00:37:41.783 --> 00:37:43.250
What are you charging me with?

00:37:43.285 --> 00:37:45.310
Collaborating with the enemy,

00:37:45.354 --> 00:37:48.414
which, in the Continuum,
is a crime punishable...

00:37:48.457 --> 00:37:49.515
by death.

00:38:11.813 --> 00:38:13.405
- Captain.
- Private.

00:38:13.448 --> 00:38:14.415
Let's go.

00:38:14.449 --> 00:38:15.746
Why won't you listen to me?

00:38:15.784 --> 00:38:17.046
I told your commander
last night,

00:38:17.085 --> 00:38:19.417
we can resolve
the situation peacefully.

00:38:21.657 --> 00:38:24.023
If it's any consolation,
there are those in the Continuum

00:38:24.059 --> 00:38:25.924
who will remember us as martyrs.

00:38:26.028 --> 00:38:28.121
I'd rather skip
that particular honor.

00:38:29.965 --> 00:38:30.932
Oh...

00:38:30.999 --> 00:38:33.729
Still, you have to admit
there's something romantic

00:38:33.769 --> 00:38:36.169
about going
to our deaths together.

00:38:39.174 --> 00:38:41.870
Do you have any last words?

00:38:41.910 --> 00:38:44.276
I won't plead for my own life.

00:38:44.313 --> 00:38:47.612
From your perspective,
I know it seems insignificant,

00:38:47.649 --> 00:38:49.310
but what is not insignificant

00:38:49.351 --> 00:38:51.911
is the fact that the Q,
as an omnipotent race,

00:38:51.954 --> 00:38:54.855
have an opportunity
to be a positive force,

00:38:54.890 --> 00:38:57.916
to set a higher standard
for other beings in the galaxy.

00:38:57.960 --> 00:39:01.987
I implore you all
don't go through with this.

00:39:02.030 --> 00:39:03.327
Don't allow yourselves

00:39:03.365 --> 00:39:05.993
to continue using violence
to resolve your differences.

00:39:07.202 --> 00:39:09.534
Q, do you have anything to add?

00:39:13.008 --> 00:39:16.500
Today, I sacrifice my existence
for the principles

00:39:16.545 --> 00:39:22.484
of freedom and individuality
that I have fought for so long.

00:39:22.517 --> 00:39:25.918
But this woman is innocent.

00:39:25.954 --> 00:39:29.117
What's more she saved my life

00:39:29.157 --> 00:39:32.524
and she tried to save us
from each other.

00:39:32.561 --> 00:39:34.222
Kill me if you must...

00:39:36.565 --> 00:39:38.260
but let her go.

00:39:38.300 --> 00:39:41.360
It's a very touching speech, Q.

00:39:41.403 --> 00:39:45.066
But as usual, your rhetoric
fails to compensate

00:39:45.107 --> 00:39:47.234
for your irresponsibility.

00:40:03.759 --> 00:40:04.748
Ready.

00:40:08.530 --> 00:40:09.462
Aim.

00:40:15.137 --> 00:40:16.832
I'm sorry.

00:40:18.240 --> 00:40:19.730
I know.

00:40:20.976 --> 00:40:22.910
Fire!

00:40:22.944 --> 00:40:23.911
I'm hit.

00:40:24.980 --> 00:40:26.242
I'm dying.

00:40:29.985 --> 00:40:31.748
Q.

00:40:31.787 --> 00:40:32.754
What?

00:40:32.788 --> 00:40:34.779
They're not firing at us.

00:40:34.823 --> 00:40:36.085
They're not?

00:40:49.538 --> 00:40:51.199
Harry, get to the Captain.

00:41:10.625 --> 00:41:11.819
Captain, are you all right?

00:41:11.860 --> 00:41:12.952
I'm fine.

00:41:12.994 --> 00:41:15.292
Oh, darling, I knew
you'd come for me.

00:41:15.330 --> 00:41:16.957
Aren't you going to untie me?

00:41:17.065 --> 00:41:18.464
How do I know you won't run off

00:41:18.500 --> 00:41:20.798
with the next bipedal female
that catches your eye?

00:41:20.836 --> 00:41:22.861
Well, it just so happens
I have a proposal

00:41:22.904 --> 00:41:24.963
which will reassure you
of my devotion.

00:41:25.006 --> 00:41:26.268
Hmm!

00:41:32.047 --> 00:41:33.275
Put down the gun!

00:41:45.761 --> 00:41:46.955
Think of it, Q.

00:41:46.995 --> 00:41:49.088
We'd be visionaries,
innovators...

00:41:49.131 --> 00:41:50.996
the parents of peace.

00:41:51.066 --> 00:41:53.591
Oh, that does have a ring to it.

00:41:53.635 --> 00:41:55.967
Captain, what should
I do with him?

00:41:56.004 --> 00:41:57.904
Q and I have a plan
to end the war.

00:41:57.939 --> 00:41:58.906
Call off your troops.

00:41:58.940 --> 00:42:01.170
Do as she says,
and I'll call my people off.

00:42:01.209 --> 00:42:02.870
They may be humanoids,

00:42:02.911 --> 00:42:05.243
but they're using our weapons.

00:42:06.248 --> 00:42:07.215
Cease fire!

00:42:07.249 --> 00:42:08.216
Hold your fire!

00:42:08.250 --> 00:42:09.217
Cease fire!

00:42:09.251 --> 00:42:11.151
Tell our people
to stop shooting.

00:42:11.186 --> 00:42:12.153
Hold your fire!

00:42:12.187 --> 00:42:13.779
Put down your weapons.

00:42:13.822 --> 00:42:15.790
So, darling, have you
given any thought

00:42:15.824 --> 00:42:16.950
as to how we might accomplish

00:42:17.025 --> 00:42:19.357
this historic act
of procreation?

00:42:19.394 --> 00:42:21.362
I've thought of nothing else
since you suggested it.

00:42:21.396 --> 00:42:22.363
Oh...

00:42:22.397 --> 00:42:23.523
As a matter of fact, I...

00:42:24.666 --> 00:42:25.633
Oh.

00:42:25.667 --> 00:42:27.658
Oh. Oh.

00:42:29.037 --> 00:42:30.868
I love it when you talk dirty.

00:42:30.906 --> 00:42:32.237
Why don't I give you two
some privacy?

00:42:32.274 --> 00:42:33.400
Oh, Kathy.

00:42:33.441 --> 00:42:34.908
Don't you like to watch?

00:42:43.552 --> 00:42:46.180
- Oh.
- Mmm.

00:42:47.923 --> 00:42:49.857
I was good, wasn't I?

00:42:49.891 --> 00:42:51.756
Very good.

00:42:52.794 --> 00:42:53.818
That was it?

00:42:55.397 --> 00:42:56.386
You had your chance.

00:42:56.431 --> 00:42:58.023
Don't go crying about it now.

00:43:06.508 --> 00:43:07.941
Lieutenant Paris,
what's our position?

00:43:10.946 --> 00:43:12.914
We're back
on our original course.

00:43:12.948 --> 00:43:14.939
All crew are present
and accounted for.

00:43:15.050 --> 00:43:18.417
Ensign Kim,
any sign of supernovas?

00:43:19.888 --> 00:43:21.116
No, ma'am.

00:43:21.156 --> 00:43:22.851
Nothing but calm space ahead.

00:43:22.891 --> 00:43:24.950
Looks like the war's over.

00:43:26.394 --> 00:43:30.956
Mr. Chakotay, run a series
of standard diagnostics.

00:43:31.032 --> 00:43:34.433
If everything checks out,
take us to warp 6.

00:43:34.469 --> 00:43:35.800
Aye, Captain.

00:43:35.837 --> 00:43:37.828
I'll be in my ready room.

00:43:41.176 --> 00:43:42.200
A-dabba-dabba-do.

00:43:44.246 --> 00:43:45.213
Q.

00:43:45.247 --> 00:43:47.340
He's got my cheekbones,
don't you think?

00:43:47.382 --> 00:43:48.872
He's adorable.

00:43:52.420 --> 00:43:54.888
I'd say fatherhood
agrees with you.

00:43:54.923 --> 00:43:57.983
Well, I'll admit, I...
I look at the universe

00:43:58.059 --> 00:43:59.993
in an entirely
different way now.

00:44:00.095 --> 00:44:02.154
I mean, I can't go around

00:44:02.197 --> 00:44:05.689
causing temporal anomalies
or subspace inversions

00:44:05.734 --> 00:44:08.931
without considering the impact
it'll have on my son.

00:44:09.037 --> 00:44:11.631
I'm glad to hear you intend
to set a good example.

00:44:11.673 --> 00:44:14.904
By the way, did I tell you
how smart he is?

00:44:14.943 --> 00:44:16.376
I've already taught him

00:44:16.411 --> 00:44:19.175
how to knock small planets
out of orbit.

00:44:19.214 --> 00:44:21.114
And I thought you were
going to teach him

00:44:21.149 --> 00:44:22.377
about love and conscience.

00:44:22.417 --> 00:44:23.509
Oh...

00:44:23.551 --> 00:44:25.951
that's why we want Aunty Kathy

00:44:26.021 --> 00:44:28.683
to be the godmother now,
don't we?

00:44:30.425 --> 00:44:32.393
I'm... honored.

00:44:32.427 --> 00:44:35.658
Yeah, well, wait until
we ask you to baby-sit.

00:44:35.697 --> 00:44:39.258
You can't leave the little guy
alone for a nanosecond.

00:44:39.301 --> 00:44:43.499
Well... it's time to be going.

00:44:43.538 --> 00:44:48.100
The old ball and chain
really hates it when we're late.

00:44:48.143 --> 00:44:49.508
Say bye-bye.

00:44:52.147 --> 00:44:53.671
Bye-bye.
